{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>When you come to the land of your dwellings, etc.</b> Because HaShem saw the sickness of their hearts in the decree of their wandering in the wilderness for forty years, far removed from entering the land, therefore He sustained their hearts with commandments dependent on the land, to establish their spirit that they would go up and inherit their land, and the great length of time would not harm something held certain to come. And He was precise to say <b>which I am giving to you</b> — even though that generation's corpses would fall in the wilderness, all the people who went out from Egypt aged twenty and above — this comes to say that the deed of children is also attributed to the fathers, for He established their children in their stead." "<b>Further,</b> it appears one may say that His saying <b>I am giving to you</b> follows the statement of our Sages of blessed memory (Sanhedrin 90b): From where do we derive the resurrection of the dead from the Torah? For it is written ״אֲשֶׁר נִשְׁבַּע ה׳ לַאֲבוֹתֵיכֶם לָתֵת לָהֶם״ (Exodus 6:4) — ״to you״ is not stated but ״to them,״ and so forth. Likewise here He promised them that they would arise in the resurrection of the dead and inherit their land."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:09:42.938919028Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}